00:19:23.000 --> 00:19:28.000
So, what I'm saying is, it's the parent's responsibility. If the mother is setting the example for the daughter...

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:36.000
Eric: Is there anything wrong with getting pregnant with a kid?

00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:41.000
Eric: Maybe they got married in their way in front of God.

00:19:42.000 --> 00:19:43.000
Dr. Khalifa: There's no such thing.

00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:44.000
Eric: Okay.

00:19:48.000 --> 00:19:52.000
Dr. Khalifa: You mean there's nothing wrong with dropping out of school at the age of 15 and getting pregnant?

00:19:52.000 --> 00:20:08.000
Eric: No, I mean, school is not a compulsory thing in itself. For...

00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:14.000
Dr. Khalifa: So, you think it's okay to drop out of school and go to the boyfriend and get pregnant without marriage?

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:18.000
Eric: I didn't say that without marriage. I said maybe with marriage.

00:20:19.000 --> 00:20:23.000
Dr. Khalifa: Well, so why not get married?

00:20:24.000 --> 00:20:26.000
Eric: I don't know if they got married. Dr. Khalifa: At 15 years old. Pardon?

00:20:26.000 --> 00:20:28.000
Eric: Maybe they...they...

00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:37.000
Dr. Khalifa: Why marry in secret? There's a girl 15 years old in school. She drops out, goes to her boyfriend and she marries him and gets pregnant. Why not make the marriage public?

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:45.000
Eric: I don't know if they made it public or not. But what I'm saying is that, Rashad, rules are such.

00:20:45.000 --> 00:20:46.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:20:46.000 --> 00:20:52.000
Eric: It's not a criteria for righteousness. I didn't find in the Quran that we have to go to school.

00:20:52.000 --> 00:20:54.000
Dr. Khalifa: Maybe it is. You didn't read the Quran.

00:20:54.000 --> 00:20:55.000
Eric: Maybe she was tired.

00:20:55.000 --> 00:20:57.000
Dr. Khalifa: You didn't read the Quran.

00:20:58.000 --> 00:21:04.000
You have to read the Quran. It tells you, we were talking about this two days ago, that the rich believer is better than the poor believer.

00:21:05.000 --> 00:21:07.000
That's what God is saying. What does this mean?

00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:11.000
Eric: Yeah, that's the more educated that they are. Dr. Khalifa: Right.

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:14.000
Dr. Khalifa: In fact, I will let you read it.

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:23.000
Eric: In many schools, they are teaching, they are indoctrinating.

00:21:24.000 --> 00:21:26.000
Dr. Khalifa: Indoctrinating what?

00:21:27.000 --> 00:21:30.000
Eric: Well, in materialist values and in...

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:32.000
Dr. Khalifa: So, do you suggest that we cancel schools?

00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:41.000
Eric: No, we can improve schools. But if some young people drop out of school, maybe it's a reaction against that they don't believe with what is...

00:21:43.000 --> 00:21:46.000
Eric: The schools are under chosens' control, but they don't...

00:21:49.000 --> 00:21:51.000
Dr. Khalifa: Look at page 275.

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:57.000
If you read for us 75 and 76, you'll appreciate it.

00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:00.000
Dr. Khalifa: My pillow.

00:22:17.000 --> 00:22:22.000
You can read the Quran. When I said "you didn't read the Quran", it means you read it, but you didn't read it.

00:22:23.000 --> 00:22:27.000
Dr. Khalifa: Because when you make a statement like that... Eric: But that's easy to say. That's easy to say.

00:22:27.000 --> 00:22:29.000
Eric: I didn't make a statement. I made a question.

00:22:29.000 --> 00:22:33.000
Dr. Khalifa: You said the school is not important, or it's not mandatory. Something like that.

00:22:33.000 --> 00:22:36.000
Eric: I didn't say that knowledge is not important.

00:22:37.000 --> 00:22:38.000
Dr. Khalifa: You said school is not.

00:22:38.000 --> 00:22:43.000
Eric: I said that people who drop out of school can have very good reasons for it.

00:22:43.000 --> 00:22:45.000
Dr. Khalifa: You can't get knowledge without school, that's for sure.

00:22:45.000 --> 00:22:46.000
Eric: But I will read it.

00:22:46.000 --> 00:22:54.000
Dr. Khalifa: It will take you 20 times as long if you wanna educate yourself outside, without school.

00:22:54.000 --> 00:22:56.000
Eric: What? Why?

00:22:56.000 --> 00:22:57.000
Dr. Khalifa: I've seen both.

00:22:57.000 --> 00:23:02.000
Eric: Are you trying to say that (unintelligible) is protected?

00:23:03.000 --> 00:23:07.000
Dr. Khalifa: I didn't say that. I said "the education in school is faster than education without school."

00:23:07.000 --> 00:23:14.000
Eric: That is a simplistic generalization which has nothing to do... because each individual is different. And there are lots of individuals.

00:23:14.000 --> 00:23:19.000
Dr. Khalifa: Well, I've seen both examples. I've seen people who go to school and people who didn't go to school. A man: Yes. Yes.

00:23:19.000 --> 00:23:28.000
Dr. Khalifa: And when you go to school and you have 15 points, you study logic and philosophy and accounting and economics and journalism.

00:23:28.000 --> 00:23:32.000
But if you do it on your own, it's gonna be 20 times as long.

00:23:32.000 --> 00:23:39.000
This has been the experience. You can accumulate the experience of a hundred scholars because...

00:23:39.000 --> 00:23:41.000
A woman: I agree because... Dr. Khalifa: There, she agrees. Yes.

00:23:41.000 --> 00:23:48.000
Dr. Khalifa: You can look at a research that did a lot of surveys, surveyed thousands of people, and come up with a conclusion.

00:23:48.000 --> 00:23:53.000
Eric: But you see, the school is not the guarantee that you will learn the right thing. And...

00:23:53.000 --> 00:23:54.000
Dr. Khalifa: Ignorance is?

00:23:56.000 --> 00:24:01.000
Eric: Well, your mother, for instance, she was not that ignorant. She wanted to know more, but she told you the truth.

00:24:01.000 --> 00:24:02.000
Eric: to worship God alone. Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:10.000
Eric: You see, don't mix up things like this, because the facts that you have about the school is not the guarantee that

00:24:10.000 --> 00:24:14.000
Eric: that you will succeed in life. Dr. Khalifa: So, this proves that ignorance is good.

00:24:14.000 --> 00:24:16.000
Eric: No, I didn't say that. Dr. Khalifa: What are you saying?

00:24:16.000 --> 00:24:21.000
Eric: No, I'm saying that... I'm saying... I'm saying... Dr. Khalifa: You're saying the school doesn't guarantee happiness, therefore let us cancel schools.

00:24:21.000 --> 00:24:25.000
Eric: What I'm trying to say... I don't support... I don't want to start an argument. Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:24:26.000 --> 00:24:32.000
Dr. Khalifa: I'm repeating what you're saying. You're saying "the school does not guarantee happiness", right?

00:24:32.000 --> 00:24:33.000
Dr. Khalifa: Is this what you said? He says Eric: Yes.

00:24:34.000 --> 00:24:36.000
Dr. Khalifa: "Therefore, let us eliminate schools."

00:24:36.000 --> 00:24:37.000
Eric: No, I didn't say that.

00:24:37.000 --> 00:24:38.000
Dr. Khalifa: Okay, what are you saying?

00:24:39.000 --> 00:24:40.000
Dr. Khalifa: What is your conclusion?

00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:50.000
Eric: My conclusion is that we know very well that the school system today is not optimal.

00:24:51.000 --> 00:24:53.000
Eric: Or do you think it is? Dr. Khalifa: Well, it's the best.

00:24:53.000 --> 00:24:55.000
Dr. Khalifa: The best ever. Eric: You think it's the best? Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:24:55.000 --> 00:24:58.000
A woman: (unintelligible) Eric: Hold on.

00:24:58.000 --> 00:24:59.000
Dr. Khalifa: It's the best ever.

00:24:59.000 --> 00:25:01.000
A man: What school are you talking about?

00:25:01.000 --> 00:25:05.000
Dr. Khalifa: Any school system anywhere in the world today is better than any other time.

00:25:06.000 --> 00:25:08.000
Eric: You believe that sincerely? Dr. Khalifa: Yes, I know that.

00:25:08.000 --> 00:25:17.000
Eric: Well, I don't want to discuss this, but there is a national emergency plan in the United States because the people don't learn anything in the school.

00:25:17.000 --> 00:25:23.000
And the level of illiteracy and the level of Analphabetism has increased in the United States.

00:25:23.000 --> 00:25:26.000
Eric: So I think this is a little bit... Dr. Khalifa: Why?

00:25:26.000 --> 00:25:32.000
Eric: Because the schools don't teach anymore as they used to.

00:25:32.000 --> 00:25:33.000
They don't teach.

00:25:33.000 --> 00:25:37.000
Dr. Khalifa: Well, they are better than... Eric: They have acquired new so-called

00:25:37.000 --> 00:25:42.000
Eric: methods which are not as good teaching methods as they used to be.

00:25:42.000 --> 00:25:43.000
Dr. Khalifa: So, what do you suggest?

00:25:43.000 --> 00:25:55.000
Eric: And the children are not very motivated when they go to school because there are a lot of other activities that are promoted on the side.

00:25:55.000 --> 00:26:06.000
And the role of the school today has become more of a social institution to teach young children to socialize rather than to acquire knowledge. And maybe this...

00:26:06.000 --> 00:26:09.000
Dr. Khalifa: Somehow Eric has taken us away from the Quran. Is this true?

00:26:09.000 --> 00:26:11.000
A man: Yes. Dr. Khalifa: Ok.

00:26:11.000 --> 00:26:15.000
Dr. Khalifa: We'd like to study the Quran and not politics or school systems or...

00:26:15.000 --> 00:26:17.000
Eric: Yes, but you took (unintelligible) Dr. Khalifa: Our children...

00:26:17.000 --> 00:26:19.000
Dr. Khalifa: Our children are the most educated kids in the world.

00:26:19.000 --> 00:26:23.000
Eric: You are just knocking off this 15 or 16-year-old girl or whatever.

00:26:23.000 --> 00:26:26.000
Just like this. Maybe she has a very good reason.

00:26:26.000 --> 00:26:32.000
Dr. Khalifa: We uphold the highest, we uphold the highest moral character because God told us to do so.

00:26:32.000 --> 00:26:38.000
If a girl gets pregnant, 15, first of all, physiologically she's not ready to get pregnant. It is not good for her.

00:26:38.000 --> 00:26:41.000
To drop out of school is not good for her. It is a bad example.

00:26:42.000 --> 00:26:48.000
And it affects your behavior.

00:26:49.000 --> 00:26:55.000
When you don't have the highest moral standard, it affects your behavior and then it affects you.

00:26:55.000 --> 00:26:57.000
Eric: Maybe this girl was a believer.

00:26:57.000 --> 00:26:58.000
Dr. Khalifa: Pardon?

00:26:58.000 --> 00:26:59.000
Dr. Khalifa: Maybe this girl was a believer.

00:26:59.000 --> 00:27:01.000
Eric: Maybe she's... Dr. Khalifa: No, she's not a believer.

00:27:01.000 --> 00:27:06.000
Dr. Khalifa: She doesn't know anything. She's drugged. She's an alcoholic. She's a 15-year-old pregnant without marriage.

00:27:07.000 --> 00:27:11.000
Dr. Khalifa: How can she be a believer when she got pregnant at 15 and dropped out of school? Eric: I don't know.

00:27:11.000 --> 00:27:15.000
Dr. Khalifa: Tell it to her mother. I mean, why do you think she's a believer? Because she got pregnant?

00:27:15.000 --> 00:27:18.000
Eric: I said maybe she is. How do you know that she's not?

00:27:19.000 --> 00:27:20.000
Dr. Khalifa: Alright.

00:27:20.000 --> 00:27:28.000
A woman: How you're saying, how you're saying like (unintelligible)?

00:27:28.000 --> 00:27:32.000
Eric: I'm trying to say that God knows but we don't know.

00:27:32.000 --> 00:27:36.000
Dr. Khalifa: So, a girl... Ok, Eric... Eric: We shouldn't pretend that we know, because God knows.

00:27:36.000 --> 00:27:42.000
Dr. Khalifa: So, the girl that gets pregnant, drops out of school at 15, and with her boyfriend and pregnant, she has a child.

00:27:43.000 --> 00:27:49.000
Dr. Khalifa: This is a criterion for a believer. This tells us she's a believer. Is this true? Is this what you're saying?

00:27:49.000 --> 00:27:51.000
Eric: What are you saying?

00:27:51.000 --> 00:28:00.000
Dr. Khalifa: A girl that's 15 years old, drops out of school and gets pregnant and gives birth to a child out of wedlock. This is a sign of a believer.

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:02.000
Eric: I didn't say that.

00:28:03.000 --> 00:28:04.000
Dr. Khalifa: You said "maybe she's a believer."

00:28:04.000 --> 00:28:07.000
Eric: I said "maybe she's a believer." Dr. Khalifa: Because all the signs are there.

00:28:08.000 --> 00:28:11.000
Dr. Khalifa: All the signs of a believer are there. Right?

00:28:12.000 --> 00:28:14.000
Eric: Why do you say that all signs of a believer are there?

00:28:14.000 --> 00:28:15.000
Dr. Khalifa: Well, this is your conclusion. Eric: No.

00:28:15.000 --> 00:28:20.000
Dr. Khalifa: You must see signs. Tell me. Why "Maybe she's a believer"? Why? Eric: I didn't draw any conclusions. Don't put words in my mouth, Rashad.

00:28:21.000 --> 00:28:27.000
Eric: I'm just trying to say that what she has in her heart, for whom we don't know.

00:28:27.000 --> 00:28:31.000
Dr. Khalifa: Well, I think you're bad influence on us, Eric, and I think, I suggest you go back to Switzerland.

00:28:32.000 --> 00:28:34.000
That's my suggestion.

00:28:34.000 --> 00:28:39.000
Because your behavior reflects what you're saying, and it hasn't been very good.

00:28:41.000 --> 00:28:44.000
Eric: I'm sorry. Dr. Khalifa: Me too.

00:28:47.000 --> 00:28:50.000
Dr. Khalifa: I know certain things you don't know, so excuse my expression.

00:28:50.000 --> 00:28:57.000
A woman: If something happened like we did say, we as believers judge it from what the Quran says.

00:28:57.000 --> 00:29:06.000
But not to judge the person for what she knows. That's what she decides to do if she knew better.

00:29:07.000 --> 00:29:14.000
If she knew about the rules and regulations, that regulation she would not have been in that position.

00:29:14.000 --> 00:29:15.000
Dr. Khalifa: That's right.

00:29:15.000 --> 00:29:20.000
A woman: Because she is in that position from what she knows.

00:29:20.000 --> 00:29:27.000
But from what we know, and even for me as a woman, I would not wanna be pregnant very soon.

00:29:28.000 --> 00:29:30.000
I mean, it's a serious responsibility.

00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:35.000
Dr. Khalifa: No, I mean, looking from God's point of view, strictly from God's point of view,

00:29:35.000 --> 00:29:40.000
I don't think it's a good influence when we have here children, boys and girls, to hear somebody say

00:29:40.000 --> 00:29:45.000
"maybe she's a believer", when she got pregnant at 15 and dropped out of school, and so on.

00:29:45.000 --> 00:29:50.000
A woman: But I have... Dr. Khalifa: So, I'm very jealous when it comes to guarding our standards.

00:29:50.000 --> 00:29:54.000
A woman: But I have another question that I can add to that.

00:29:54.000 --> 00:29:59.000
As human beings, we all have to have feelings for the baby.

00:29:59.000 --> 00:30:05.000
I mean, the mother.... the baby....

00:30:05.000 --> 00:30:06.000
Dr. Khalifa: Say it again.

00:30:07.000 --> 00:30:10.000
A woman: (unintelligible)

00:30:10.000 --> 00:30:18.000
A woman: Because I know in our country, I mean, I know in our law, if even a man and a woman get pregnant

00:30:18.000 --> 00:30:21.000
and want to get married after one month...

00:30:24.000 --> 00:30:30.000
A woman: I mean, if they have a baby and after one month, they wanna get married, that child is caught in this situation.

00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:33.000
A woman: Do you agree, (unintelligible)? Dr. Khalifa: Yes. Eric: Yes.

00:30:37.000 --> 00:30:42.000
Dr. Khalifa: It was conceived outside of marriage, which is God's institution.

00:30:47.000 --> 00:30:50.000
I just don't trust you talking to the believers when I'm not here.

00:30:52.000 --> 00:30:53.000
I'm not comfortable.

00:30:53.000 --> 00:30:58.000
Dr. Khalifa: Because of your point of view, maybe you have some European ideas or something. Eric: Dr., I'm not promoting...No.

00:30:58.000 --> 00:31:03.000
Dr. Khalifa: Whatever it is, I'm not comfortable when you're talking to the people and there's always some negative feedback.

00:31:05.000 --> 00:31:12.000
So, I'd appreciate it if you just visit when I'm here, or it'd be better if you just go back to Switzerland.

00:31:17.000 --> 00:31:19.000
Are there any other questions on this?

00:31:20.000 --> 00:31:22.000
What were we talking about?

00:31:24.000 --> 00:31:26.000
I was saying that the parents set the example for the children.

00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:31.000
A man: Yes.

00:31:34.000 --> 00:31:37.000
A man: There's a good example from Maryam and,...

00:31:37.000 --> 00:31:39.000
Dr. Khalifa: (19:20) وَلَمْ أَكُ بَغِيًّۭا

00:31:39.000 --> 00:31:41.000
A man: 19 years old.

00:31:43.000 --> 00:31:45.000
Dr. Khalifa: (unintelligible)

00:31:45.000 --> 00:31:46.000
Yeah. Beautiful.

00:31:46.000 --> 00:31:50.000
A man: Mary was 19 years old when she said "no man has ever touched me."

00:31:50.000 --> 00:31:52.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes. That's the Quranic lesson, yes.

00:31:52.000 --> 00:31:54.000
A man: (unintelligible)

00:31:54.000 --> 00:31:56.000
A woman: (unintelligible)

00:31:58.000 --> 00:32:06.000
Dr. Khalifa: There is a good hint when it is in Sura 19 and it's entitled "Maryam" and it tells the birth of Jesus and so on.

00:32:06.000 --> 00:32:08.000
It's a very good indication.

00:32:11.000 --> 00:32:16.000
15 is just... even physiologically, the girl is not ready.

00:32:16.000 --> 00:32:25.000
Just because she's menstruating and so on doesn't mean the uterus is ready and emotional, psychological conditions are satisfied.

00:32:27.000 --> 00:32:28.000
And the same with the boys.

00:32:28.000 --> 00:32:33.000
A woman: I was just trying to give the whole context of this.

00:32:33.000 --> 00:32:35.000
Maybe we'll learn that later.

00:32:36.000 --> 00:32:42.000
Fifteen or sixteen (unintelligible)

00:32:42.000 --> 00:32:47.000
Because they have a child, I believe they have a (unintelligible) life.

00:32:48.000 --> 00:32:50.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes, infant mortality.

00:32:50.000 --> 00:32:51.000
A woman: (unintelligible)

00:32:51.000 --> 00:32:52.000
Dr. Khalifa: What a mistake!

00:32:52.000 --> 00:32:58.000
A woman: 1, 2, 3, Two brothers and a sister died before me. I was a small child.

00:32:59.000 --> 00:33:01.000
A woman: Because my mother was very young.

00:33:01.000 --> 00:33:02.000
Dr. Khalifa: Right.

00:33:04.000 --> 00:33:09.000
Dr. Khalifa: Just physiologically, the boys and the girls are not ready before the age of 19 or 20.

00:33:11.000 --> 00:33:16.000
A woman: So, they didn't know in advance and now they are, you know, dying young.

00:33:17.000 --> 00:33:25.000
A woman: (unintelligible)

00:33:25.000 --> 00:33:28.000
A woman: They are talking about hormones. A woman: (unintelligible)

00:33:28.000 --> 00:33:33.000
A woman: Well, I know there are hormones. But we have a brain, too. A woman: (unintelligible)

00:33:33.000 --> 00:33:36.000
A woman: The animals (unintelligible) A woman: (unintelligible)

00:33:36.000 --> 00:33:38.000
Dr. Khalifa: Animals are better. A woman: (unintelligible) normal.

00:33:38.000 --> 00:33:44.000
A woman: I mean, animals are better because they know when they are ready.

00:33:48.000 --> 00:33:55.000
A woman: It's a very hard concept for the Westerners. I understand what you are talking about. Please, I mean, please.

00:33:56.000 --> 00:34:03.000
A woman: I mean, but, I mean, I don't picture any of my children running around with a normal kind of dog.

00:34:05.000 --> 00:34:10.000
A woman: That's not human nature. I don't want my daughter or my son are engaged.

00:34:11.000 --> 00:34:13.000
A woman: I want them to learn.

00:34:13.000 --> 00:34:16.000
Dr. Khalifa: Control themselves. A woman: Have self-control.

00:34:16.000 --> 00:34:18.000
Dr. Khalifa: Right. A woman: This is what it's all about.

00:34:18.000 --> 00:34:21.000
A woman: (unintelligible) And that is the heart. Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:34:21.000 --> 00:34:23.000
A woman: People that feel normal. People that...

00:34:24.000 --> 00:34:31.000
Dr. Khalifa: It seems like in the last ten Quranic studies, I have been reminding the parents to tell their children that they are very special.

00:34:31.000 --> 00:34:35.000
They must learn they are very special. They are not to behave like the commoners.

00:34:36.000 --> 00:34:41.000
And they must not let anybody touch them in a sexual manner until their wedding night.

00:34:41.000 --> 00:34:44.000
And yes, I have an appendix here entitled "Virginity."

00:34:44.000 --> 00:34:48.000
So, if you are too embarrassed, you can just have them read the appendix.

00:34:49.000 --> 00:34:53.000
Sometimes it's a ticklish subject. It's difficult to discuss.

00:34:54.000 --> 00:35:00.000
But they must teach them first that their happiness in this life and forever depends on obeying God's commandments.

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:04.000
A woman: Well, I was in a family conference. I mean, it was a service. Dr. Khalifa: And...

00:35:05.000 --> 00:35:10.000
A woman: How it was (unintelligible). And at the end, he said "oh yes, they were talking about something called hormones."

00:35:10.000 --> 00:35:12.000
A woman: But what about the men? Dr. Khalifa: Right.

00:35:12.000 --> 00:35:15.000
A woman: And it was in expression of "don't let women touch the men", you know.

00:35:16.000 --> 00:35:22.000
A woman: And on and on. And after he was taking (unintelligible), and I said "this is between men and women. Dr. Khalifa: Right.

00:35:22.000 --> 00:35:27.000
A woman: (unintelligible) He was serious. (unintelligible).

00:35:27.000 --> 00:35:28.000
Dr. Khalifa: For both. A woman: (unintellgibile)

00:35:28.000 --> 00:35:33.000
A woman: But I'm not having to blame him. It's not because the woman is sure (unintelligible).

00:35:33.000 --> 00:35:48.000
A woman: The man didn't do anything, I mean (unintelligible)

00:35:50.000 --> 00:35:55.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yep. This is why I put in the headlines that boys and girls.

00:35:55.000 --> 00:35:57.000
Because there is no double standard there.

00:36:02.000 --> 00:36:07.000
You know, first and foremost, if a person is a believer, the children are in God's hands.

00:36:09.000 --> 00:36:10.000
And you must have that confidence.

00:36:15.000 --> 00:36:18.000
Just one. Roxana was asking the same question.

