01:18:01.000 --> 01:18:04.000
Azar: In Sura 2, verse 29, we read,

01:18:04.000 --> 01:18:15.000
[2:29] He is the One who created for you everything on earth, then turned to the sky and created seven universes therein,* and He is fully aware of all things.

01:18:16.000 --> 01:18:24.000
And this question come up that, in another verse, we read that everything was in masses and then

01:18:24.000 --> 01:18:27.000
explosion happened and there was, you know, everything was created.

01:18:28.000 --> 01:18:35.000
And when I think about that and I read this one, I am confused that the earth was

01:18:35.000 --> 01:18:37.000
Azar: created first and then the seven heavens.

01:18:37.000 --> 01:18:42.000
Dr. Khalifa: The provisions for every ant, horse and mouse were calculated.

01:18:42.000 --> 01:18:44.000
The design was done.

01:18:44.000 --> 01:18:46.000
Everything was created first.

01:18:46.000 --> 01:18:50.000
Then... but the process of creation is the big bang.

01:18:51.000 --> 01:18:54.000
Azar: So, this is just the provisions that creates...

01:18:54.000 --> 01:19:01.000
Dr. Khalifa: The earth, the earth took four days. I mean, design and calculate the provisions and everything.

01:19:03.000 --> 01:19:05.000
A woman: 4 days for the...

01:19:05.000 --> 01:19:06.000
Dr. Khalifa: Just the earth.

01:19:06.000 --> 01:19:07.000
A woman: Just the earth.

01:19:07.000 --> 01:19:10.000
Dr. Khalifa: (41:10) وَقَدَّرَ فِيهَآ أَقْوَٰتَهَا فِىٓ أَرْبَعَةِ أَيَّامٍۢ

01:19:12.000 --> 01:19:18.000
See? God created the whole universe... This is in Sura 41, verse 11.

01:19:20.000 --> 01:19:29.000
Edip: Rashad, Thumma (ثُمَّ) in Arabic, doesn't feel, in Quran, creation doesn't mean always a time sequence. Dr. Khalifa: Right.

01:19:29.000 --> 01:19:31.000
Sometimes, it is like this.

01:19:32.000 --> 01:19:35.000
Dr. Khalifa: As a matter of fact, there is no time sequence. As far as God is concerned, there's no time.

01:19:36.000 --> 01:19:38.000
Edip: To show us, even to teach us. Dr. Khalifa: Yep. Everything existed.

01:19:39.000 --> 01:19:44.000
Edip: No, 14, 15, to teach us sometimes God's time sequences.

01:19:44.000 --> 01:19:46.000
Dr. Khalifa: There's no time sequence for God. Edip: But... Yes.

01:19:46.000 --> 01:19:48.000
Dr. Khalifa: Did you hear that, Azar?

01:19:49.000 --> 01:19:51.000
Dr. Khalifa: Did you hear that? Azar: No, I...

01:19:51.000 --> 01:19:51.000
Dr. Khalifa: Go ahead.

01:19:52.000 --> 01:20:01.000
Edip: Here, especially in verse 29, there is no time sequence because Thumma (ثُمَّ) here, in fact,

01:20:01.000 --> 01:20:09.000
means "additionally, He created, how do you say, seven universes and He expanded them."

01:20:09.000 --> 01:20:11.000
He created this and also this.

01:20:12.000 --> 01:20:14.000
Thumma (ثُمَّ) doesn't mean, "then" doesn't mean.

01:20:14.000 --> 01:20:16.000
Edip: Here it is translated as "then."

01:20:16.000 --> 01:20:23.000
Dr. Khalifa: So, there's no time sequence for God. In other words, before the seven universes were created, God knew that the earth will be created, that Azar will be born

01:20:23.000 --> 01:20:27.000
and will move to San Francisco and will marry Mehdi at Masjid Tucson. God knew that.

01:20:27.000 --> 01:20:32.000
So, it was already created, even though there is nothing yet, as far as we're concerned.

01:20:32.000 --> 01:20:34.000
So, there is no time sequence as far as God is concerned.

01:20:34.000 --> 01:20:41.000
Azar: I said maybe, for example, you build one, the building, and you didn't finish the design,

01:20:41.000 --> 01:20:47.000
but you go first to your room and you finish this for design.

01:20:47.000 --> 01:20:49.000
Azar: Furniture and go back...

01:20:49.000 --> 01:20:53.000
Dr. Khalifa: You know in your head how many rooms you're gonna have, what it will look like.

01:20:54.000 --> 01:21:00.000
Edip: Rashad, in Arabic, Meen Ba'di Zalika (مِنْ بَعْدِ ذَلِكَ) shows time sequence "after this."

01:21:00.000 --> 01:21:01.000
Edip: But Thumma (ثُمَّ)...

01:21:01.000 --> 01:21:03.000
Dr. Khalifa: And usually Meen Ba'di Zalika (مِنْ بَعْدِ ذَلِكَ) applies to people.

01:21:04.000 --> 01:21:09.000
You disbelieved Meen Ba'di Zalika (مِنْ بَعْدِ ذَلِكَ), or you believed Meen Ba'di Zalika (مِنْ بَعْدِ ذَلِكَ), or you went to another town Meen Ba'di Zalika (مِنْ بَعْدِ ذَلِكَ).

01:21:09.000 --> 01:21:12.000
Dr. Khalifa: So, it applies to the creatures, not to the Creator.

01:21:12.000 --> 01:21:15.000
As far as God is concerned, there is no time.

01:21:16.000 --> 01:21:17.000
Therefore, there is no sequence.

01:21:19.000 --> 01:21:22.000
It means that the people who will be born a hundred years from now,

01:21:22.000 --> 01:21:26.000
God already knows about this. So, are they created yet?

01:21:28.000 --> 01:21:31.000
Yes. But they are not in existence yet.

01:21:32.000 --> 01:21:34.000
Dr. Khalifa: They will be here a hundred years from now.

01:21:34.000 --> 01:21:38.000
A man: As long as we're concerned, they're not. Dr. Khalifa: Right.

01:21:38.000 --> 01:21:43.000
Dr. Khalifa: As far as we're concerned. A man: I mean, who said that past, future, and past and present and future do not exist at the same time?

01:21:44.000 --> 01:21:48.000
Dr. Khalifa: This is why God tells us about the Day of Resurrection in the past tense, as if it happened,

01:21:48.000 --> 01:21:52.000
which is true. As far as God's concerned, it happened. Everything is done.

01:21:52.000 --> 01:22:04.000
That's why when God says Satan went to Hell, nobody can say "is it possible that God will forgive Satan", because God already tells us what happened in the future.

01:22:04.000 --> 01:22:10.000
Parivash: But the word for English, everybody understands that way, because when we say

01:22:10.000 --> 01:22:18.000
"everything on earth, then turned to the sky and created seven universes, and designed seven universes,

01:22:18.000 --> 01:22:19.000
Parivash: or created? Dr. Khalifa: created.

01:22:24.000 --> 01:22:27.000
Dr. Khalifa: It doesn't matter. We shouldn't pick on these little things.

01:22:27.000 --> 01:22:29.000
We should understand that God created the earth and the heavens.

01:22:30.000 --> 01:22:33.000
Parivash: Because when people ask us, we should have an answer for that.

01:22:34.000 --> 01:22:39.000
Dr. Khalifa: Well, this is the answer. Say "why is it relevant to you whether the earth came first or Jupiter came first?"

01:22:42.000 --> 01:22:46.000
Parivash: You know, unfortunately... Dr. Khalifa: Ask them the question. When they ask you, answer the question.

01:22:46.000 --> 01:22:49.000
Dr. Khalifa: "Is it important whether Jupiter came first or the earth came first?"

01:22:51.000 --> 01:22:52.000
"Is it important to you?"

01:22:53.000 --> 01:22:59.000
